# ⚠️  WARNING: INTENTIONALLY VULNERABLE - FOR EDUCATIONAL PURPOSES ONLY ⚠️
#
# VULNERABILITY: Inadequate .dockerignore
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A proper .dockerignore should exclude ALL of the following.
# This file intentionally leaves secrets, keys, and dev artifacts exposed
# so they get copied into the Docker image — demonstrating what NOT to do.
#
# Missing exclusions (intentionally):
#   .env                  → All hardcoded API keys / DB passwords
#   config/secrets.js     → Hardcoded credentials source file
#   db/*.db               → SQLite database with PII
#   *.pem / *.key         → Any TLS/SSH private keys
#   .git/                 → Full git history (may contain leaked secrets)
#   test/ / *.test.js     → Test files with fixture credentials
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Only excluding node_modules to keep image size manageable
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# INTENTIONALLY NOT EXCLUDED (vulnerable):
# .env
# .git
# config/secrets.js
# db/*.db
# *.pem
# *.key
# *.p12
# coverage/
# .nyc_output/
